  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Women Economic Empowerment and Care  - WE-Care - Phase 5.2 in Ethiopia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ethiopian women still are lagged behind their male counterparts in getting opportunities to participate in the labour force or to engage in economic activities,  missing opportunities to attend school, social affairs, and political participation due to unpaid care and domestic work.   Oxfam WECARE project aims to increase the recognition of unpaid care and domestic work(UCDW)  in public policy; reduce heavy and time -consuming UCDW through investments in essential public services and infrastructure; redistribute the responsibility for UCDW more equally between men and women and between households and the state; and ensure that women with care responsibilities are represented in the planning and implementation of budgets and policies that affect their lives. The program works towards a just and inclusive society by recognizing, reducing, redistributing, representing, and rewarding UCDW  Oxfam WECARE Project will be engaged on the advocacy and influencing works to bring into attention the issue of unpaid care and domestic work. In addition, the project will support for establishment and strengthen different social movements on the care economy. The major beneficiaries of this project are mainly institutions including Women Rights Organizations,Youth Led Organizations, Civil Society Organizations, community based organizations and government actors who are targeting women and girls  at large. The project will be implemented by partner at the national level and Oxfam leading the capacity building and its coordination role with the planned objectives to be achieved by the end of 2026.</narrative>
  </description>
